 an engraver, designer, and embroiderer in blue, purple, and scarlet yarn and fine linen.","verse":23}],"id":"Ahisamach","label":"Ahisamach","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Ahisamach::Ahisamach::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Original complete headword and source opening identify a named person, people, or place. Promotion requires a capitalized whole name and the original article explicitly citing this same BSB verse. No arbitrary qualifier stripping or book-title inference. This citation-constrained rule was reviewed once globally; unmatched contexts remain excluded.","sourceHeadwordId":"Ahisamach","term":"Ahisamach"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Ahisamach","sourceTitle":"Ahisamach"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"altar","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":11,"href":"?bref=Exod.38.1-7","rawReference":"Exod.38.1-7"}],"ruleId":"Altar::Altar::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Altar"},"text":"Bezalel constructed the altar of burnt offering from acacia wood. It was square, five cubits long, five cubits wide, and three cubits high.","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"altar","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":11,"href":"?bref=Exod.38.1-7","rawReference":"Exod.38.1-7"}],"ruleId":"Altar::Altar::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Altar"},"text":"He made a horn at each of its four corners, so that the horns and altar were of one piece, and he overlaid the altar with bronze.","verse":2},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"altar","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":11,"href":"?bref=Exod.38.1-7","rawReference":"Exod.38.1-7"}],"ruleId":"Altar::Altar::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Altar"},"text":"He made all the altar’s utensils of bronze—its pots, shovels, sprinkling bowls, meat forks, and firepans.","verse":3},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"altar","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":11,"href":"?bref=Exod.38.1-7","rawReference":"Exod.38.1-7"}],"ruleId":"Altar::Altar::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Altar"},"text":"He made a grate of bronze mesh for the altar under its ledge, halfway up from the bottom.","verse":4},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"altar","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":11,"href":"?bref=Exod.38.1-7","rawReference":"Exod.38.1-7"}],"ruleId":"Altar::Altar::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Altar"},"text":"Then he inserted the poles into the rings on the sides of the altar for carrying it. He made the altar with boards so that it was hollow.","verse":7}],"id":"Altar","label":"altar","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Altar::Altar::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Reviewed original headword and source sense. This substantive word is admitted only where the original article explicitly cites the exact occurrence verse; ambiguous homographs and known context mismatches are separately excluded. This is selective contextual evidence, not an automatic rule for every same-spelling word.","sourceHeadwordId":"Altar","term":"Altar"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Altar","sourceTitle":"Altar"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Bezalel son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah, made everything that the LORD had commanded Moses.","verse":22}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Moses","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Moses::Moses::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Moses"},"text":"This is the inventory for the tabernacle, the tabernacle of the Testimony, as recorded at Moses’ command by the Levites under the direction of Ithamar son of Aaron the priest.","verse":21},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Moses","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Moses::Moses::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Moses"},"text":"Bezalel son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah, made everything that the LORD had commanded Moses.","verse":22}],"id":"Moses","label":"Moses","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Moses::Moses::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Moses","term":"Moses"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Moses","sourceTitle":"Moses"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"source_verified_redirect","phrase":